WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.640
"Can Cholesterol Get Too Low?"

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:13.920
On the standard American 
diet, atherosclerosis —

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:17.840
hardening of the arteries, the number
one killer of men and women —

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.640
starts in your teens.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:25.200
Investigators collected about 3,000
sets of coronary arteries and aortas —

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:30.560
the main artery in the body — from
accident, homicide, and suicide victims,

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:35.600
15 to 34 years of age, and
this is what they found.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:40.160
The fatty streaks start in our teens,
which turn into atherosclerotic plaques

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:46.320
in our 20s, which get worse in our 30s,
and can then start killing us off.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.160
In our heart, it can
cause a heart attack.

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:51.440
In our brain, 
it can cause a stroke.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.520
How common is this?

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.440
A hundred percent of the teens they
looked at already had fatty streaks

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:00.720
building up inside their arteries,
and by their early 30s,

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.280
most already had streaks
blossoming into

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:06.480
atherosclerotic plaques
bulging into their arteries.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:12.080
This is what their aortas look like
at ages 15 through 19: fatty streaks

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:15.760
building up throughout,
but no plaques yet on average.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:18.160
But the plaques start
appearing in our early 20s,

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:21.840
and get worse in our late 20s,
by which time fatty streaks

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:23.520
have infiltrated throughout,

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:28.080
and by our early 30s, our
arteries are in bad shape.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:32.000
But that's our aorta, the main artery
that plunges down through our torso

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.880
to split off into our legs. What about
the coronary arteries feeding our heart?

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:40.240
Same thing. We start out
with fatty streaks in our teens,

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:45.120
begin to see the first hint of plaque
in our early 20s, then late 20s,

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:50.880
then look at the average coronary
arteries of 30 to 34-year-olds.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:55.840
Most people in their early 30s already
have plaques in their coronary arteries.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:00.560
Atherosclerosis begins in youth.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.320
So that's why we shouldn't wait until
heart disease becomes symptomatic

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:08.720
to treat it. If it starts in youth, we
should start treating it in youth.

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:11.360
It's like if you knew you
had a cancerous tumor,

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:14.160
you wouldn't want to wait until it
grew until a certain size to treat it.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.160
Or if you had diabetes,
you wouldn't want to wait

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:19.533
until you started going blind
before you did something about it.

00:02:19.533 --> 00:02:23.600
Okay, so how do you
treat atherosclerosis?

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:28.800
You lower LDL cholesterol through
a stringent diet that is low in cholesterol

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:35.280
and saturated fat, so a diet that's
low in eggs, meat, dairy, and junk.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:39.360
If we want to stop this epidemic, we
have to alter our lifestyle accordingly,

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.760
starting as early as possible.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:45.520
Is such a radical proposal
totally impractical?

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:48.880
I mean, eating more healthfully?
Radical!

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:51.680
It would, of course, take
an all-out commitment,

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:54.400
but remember, this is
our #1 cause of death.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.000
I mean, if you're going
to commit to anything...

00:02:57.479 --> 00:03:00.480
We did pretty good with cigarettes,
slashing smoking rates,

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:03.120
and lung cancer rates
came right down.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:04.800
And yes, healthy eating is safe.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.880
According to the Academy
of Nutrition and Dietetics,

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:10.560
the largest and oldest association
of nutrition professionals in the world,

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:14.000
even strictly plant-based diets
are appropriate for all stages

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:17.920
of the lifecycle from pregnancy,
infancy, through old age.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:19.040
And if you want to learn more,

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:22.640
the Academy can suggest
a few good websites to visit.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:26.400
Curing atherosclerosis
should be the next major

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.640
cardiovascular prevention goal.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:33.760
What evidence do we have that a
life-long suppression of LDL will do it?

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:38.800
There's a genetic mutation
of a gene called PCSK9

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:42.560
that about 1 in 50 African Americans
are lucky to be born with

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:46.160
because it gives them about a 40%
lower cholesterol their whole lives.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.360
And indeed, they have
dramatically lower rates

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:53.760
of coronary artery disease to
show for it: an 88% drop in risk,

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:57.040
despite otherwise terrible
risk factors on average.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:59.200
Most had high blood pressure
and were overweight,

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:03.040
almost a third smoked,
nearly 20% had diabetes.

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:05.600
But that just goes to show
that a lifelong history

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:08.000
of reduced LDL cholesterol levels

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:11.360
significantly lowers the risk
of coronary heart disease,

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:17.200
even in the presence of multiple risk
factors. And this near-90% drop

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:19.920
in events like heart attacks or
sudden death occurred at an average

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:26.648
LDL of 100, compared to 138.
So you could get even lower than 100.

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:31.680
Hold on! Why does the lowering of
LDL cholesterol by about 40 points

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:35.600
in those with that lucky genetic mutation
reduce heart disease incidence

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:39.600
by nearly 90%, whereas that same
40-point drop with statin drugs

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:42.880
would reduce coronary heart
disease by only about 20%?

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:46.240
The most likely answer is duration.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:48.480
When it comes to
lowering LDL cholesterol,

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:53.280
it's not only how low,
but how long it's been low.

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:58.400
That's why healthy lifestyle choices
may wipe out like 90% of our risk

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:02.815
for having a heart attack, whereas
drugs may reduce it by only 20 to 30%.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:05.840
If you're getting treated with drugs
later in life, you may have to get

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:10.720
your LDL under 70 to halt the
progression of coronary atherosclerosis.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:14.240
But if we start early enough, young
enough, it may be sufficient

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:16.960
to just lower LDL cholesterol
down to 100,

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:19.840
which should be attainable
for most people.

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:23.600
That's consistent with country-by-country
data that suggested heart disease

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:27.440
would bottom out at a population
average of about 100.

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:31.360
But that's if you can
keep it down your whole life.

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:34.720
If you're just using drugs
late in life to try to stop

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:38.800
the progression of your disease, you
have to get your LDL lower than 70.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:41.280
And if you're trying to use
drugs to reverse a lifetime

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:44.240
of bad food choices,
you don't get to zero

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:47.360
until about an LDL of 55.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:50.720
And if your heart disease is so bad
you've already had a heart attack

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:53.680
but you're trying not to die
from another one, ideally

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:57.600
you might want to push
your LDL down to about 30.

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:00.240
Once you get that low,
not only would you prevent

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:02.480
any new atherosclerotic plaques,

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:05.600
but you'd also help stabilize
the plaques you already have,

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:09.040
so they're less likely to
burst open and kill you.

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:12.880
Is it even safe to have
cholesterol levels that low though?

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:17.200
In other words, can LDL
cholesterol ever be too low?

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:19.778
We'll find out next.

